  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "Confidence in leaders starts with employees seeing them as real people, trustworthy and open. When leaders reveal their trip-ups and failures, they are seen as more approachable and less arrogant. But being vulnerable isn't easy. \n\nIn [this article](<HBR_How_to_Build_Confidence_About_Showing_Vulnerability>), the author explains how to show \"confident vulnerability\" and offers three ways to open up. Confident vulnerability means that leaders can put their self-doubts to work for them.",
